/// Since 1.1. The activity log (FR-11.9): one event per call in the Activity tab of the server
/// the user is on. Needs the `activity` permission.
///
/// A pushed event shows as '<plugin> "<text>"' with the plugin's action right-aligned on its meta
/// line. Clicking that action reaches the plugin through the existing `ui-action` path with this
/// `id`, so there is no separate callback. Limits per plugin: 1 push per 10 seconds and 50 per
/// hour; text at most 128 characters, action label at most 24 characters.
interface activity {
  use types.{error};

  /// The action shown on the event.
  record action {
    /// What the user sees, e.g. 'Notify me'; at most 24 characters.
    label: string,
    /// The plugin's own id, sent back in the `ui-action` when the event is clicked.
    id: string,
  }

  /// Pushes one event into the activity log. `text` is untrusted: control characters become
  /// spaces before it is shown.
  ///
  /// Errors: `not-permitted`, `too-large`, `rate-limited`. Nothing is stored: the log lives in
  /// memory only and is discarded when the connection ends (FR-11.4).
  push: func(text: string, action: option<action>) -> result<_, error>;
}
